---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Draft privacy policy for identizen.com and the Identizen hosted services."
  noindex
>
  <div class="container-site max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <article class="prose-idz">
      <p
        class="rounded-md border border-warning-soft bg-warning-soft px-3 py-2 text-sm text-warning-soft-fg"
      >
        Draft. Not yet reviewed by counsel; will be replaced before general availability.
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">
        The short version: we designed the system so that we hold as little as possible, and nothing
        that can be used to log in as you.
      </p>

      <h2>What the public index stores</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Public keys for your identity and devices. Never private keys, seeds, or passphrases.
        </li>
        <li>A push token per device so we can deliver a challenge id (and only a challenge id).</li>
        <li>
          A rotating Bluetooth key per device so a nearby browser can find your phone. It rotates
          every 15 minutes and is resolvable only by the index.
        </li>
        <li>
          Which sites you have logged in to (as per-site identifiers), so revocation can log you out
          everywhere.
        </li>
        <li>
          Audit events: logins, approvals, denials, enrollments, revocations, with timestamps.
        </li>
        <li>An optional handle, if you choose one.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What sites receive</h2>
      <p>
        A stable per-site identifier, an opaque device id, and the authentication method used. No
        email, no name, no cross-site identifier.
      </p>

      <h2>What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        Contact-form submissions are sent to us by email and protected by Cloudflare Turnstile. We
        do not run third-party analytics or advertising scripts.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Revoke any device, session, or paired browser from the dashboard or the app. Deleting your
        last device removes your identity from the index; audit records are retained for the period
        required by law and then deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>privacy@identizen.com</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
